1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,302
Sleeping with half your brain

2
00:00:01,302 --> 00:00:02,270
sounds great,

3
00:00:02,290 --> 00:00:03,508
until you try to talk.

4
00:00:03,528 --> 00:00:04,783
Your two halves don't do

5
00:00:04,783 --> 00:00:05,833
the same jobs.

6
00:00:05,853 --> 00:00:07,183
In most right-handed people,

7
00:00:07,203 --> 00:00:08,964
language lives mainly in the

8
00:00:08,964 --> 00:00:10,154
left hemisphere.

9
00:00:10,174 --> 00:00:11,168
So with your left half

10
00:00:11,168 --> 00:00:12,964
asleep, you'd be awake,

11
00:00:12,984 --> 00:00:14,684
but you might struggle to talk.

12
00:00:14,704 --> 00:00:16,890
Or to read your homework.

13
00:00:16,910 --> 00:00:17,760
Catch two:

14
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:18,843
each half of your brain

15
00:00:18,843 --> 00:00:20,214
controls the opposite side of

16
00:00:20,214 --> 00:00:20,937
your body.

17
00:00:20,957 --> 00:00:22,229
Left half asleep?

18
00:00:22,249 --> 00:00:23,717
Your right hand gets clumsy.

19
00:00:23,737 --> 00:00:25,434
Hope you're not right-handed.

20
00:00:25,454 --> 00:00:26,154
Oh wait,

21
00:00:26,174 --> 00:00:26,686
most people are.

22
00:00:27,686 --> 00:00:28,716
Catch three:

23
00:00:28,736 --> 00:00:29,565
your eyes are wired

24
00:00:29,565 --> 00:00:31,029
differently from a dolphin's.

25
00:00:31,049 --> 00:00:32,234
About half the nerve fibers

26
00:00:32,234 --> 00:00:33,194
from each of your eyes

27
00:00:33,194 --> 00:00:34,589
cross to the other side,

28
00:00:34,609 --> 00:00:35,635
so each eye talks to

29
00:00:35,635 --> 00:00:36,917
both halves of your brain.

30
00:00:36,937 --> 00:00:38,284
One sleepy half couldn't just

31
00:00:38,284 --> 00:00:39,787
switch off one eye.

32
00:00:39,807 --> 00:00:41,503
Subscribe for more what ifs!
